WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.168
Here's a quick recap of ERAC Lite CRM — one trusted model for your long-term-care reinsurance partners, built on your feedback.

2
00:00:09.318 --> 00:00:25.230
Today, everything about a partner relationship lives in different tools — structure in spreadsheets, contacts in Outlook, treaties in a contract system, reports in Power BI, claims in the T P A's system. We pulled it into one workspace.

3
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:28.932
First — everything you asked for is now live.

4
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:51.532
We renamed counterparties to partners everywhere. Every account now has valid contacts with a primary. There's a new Account Map showing who at ERAC owns each partner. Know Your Policyholder is surfaced as its own destination. And external systems are easy to find, with connectors to Fabric and L T C Core.

5
00:00:51.682 --> 00:01:15.106
By the numbers: eleven partners — six cedents, four T P As, and one hybrid. One hundred percent of accounts now carry contacts and a primary. Thirty-plus reinsurance records across treaties, reserves, ratings, risk and disputes. And the experience is roughly ninety percent automation, with insights surfaced proactively.

6
00:01:15.256 --> 00:01:44.584
Inside the app: a partner relationship map for structure and coverage. A 360 card that adapts to whether you're looking at a cedent or a T P A. The reinsurance backbone — treaties, reserve adequacy, partnership ratings, risk, and disputes. Projects and strategy, with a strategy agent your own team runs. And analytics — portfolio analytics, Know Your Policyholder, and a partnership and risk drill-down.

7
00:01:44.734 --> 00:02:06.886
The key point: this is about ninety percent automation, with A I surfacing insight proactively. Role-based security means the right people see the right notes. Each user gets a personal menu. And it connects into Fabric and your L T C Core warehouse. One trusted model, one workspace, for the whole team.

8
00:02:07.036 --> 00:02:16.492
Your structure, your partners, your analytics — in one workspace. We'd love your feedback: what would make this indispensable for your team?
